{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793516336,"nonce":"FBREeFxtqKm+a+4E2YGxnySWF4I=","title":"Release hygiene: screenshots, feature docs and a CHANGELOG, checked per tagged release","message":"Owner 2026-11-01: \"verifying screenshots and updating them post each tagged release as well as updating docs with newer features and changelog maintenance in a place\".\n\nToday:\n- Screenshots: docs/assets/screenshots/ (README) and ui/scarab-docs-ui/public (docs site). Last refreshed by hand in PR #48 with a temporary Vite mock mode; `just ui-mock` (VITE_SCARAB_MOCK, ui/scarab-web-ui/src/mock.ts, the acme fixture) now exists. Nothing checks that they match the current UI, so they drift with every UI PR (e.g. #61's ADR-0076 screens are not in them).\n- Feature docs: written per PR when someone remembers; no check that a release's features have a docs page.\n- Changelog: none in the tree. Release notes live only in GitHub Release bodies (written by hand per tag; v0.3.0's draft is in a session scratchpad). release.yml uploads libs-manifest.json but writes no notes.\n\nProposed:\n1. CHANGELOG.md at the repo root (Keep a Changelog layout: Unreleased + one section per tag, Upgrading / New / Fixes like the v0.2.2 and v0.3.0 notes). Each user-visible PR adds a line under Unreleased. On a tag, release.yml takes that tag's section as the GitHub Release body, so notes live in one place and the release page is generated from it. Backfill v0.1.0–v0.3.0 from the existing release bodies.\n2. Screenshots as a recipe: `just screenshots` drives `just ui-mock` with Playwright (already used by `just ui-e2e`) and writes every documented screen at fixed sizes, light and dark, into the two asset dirs. Run it before each tag; the release checklist fails if the diff of a fresh capture against the committed images is non-empty (pixel diff with a small tolerance), so drift is caught at release time, not by eye.\n3. Feature docs check per release: the release checklist lists the Unreleased CHANGELOG entries and requires each \"New\" entry to link a docs page (docs site path); a missing link fails the checklist.\n4. A release checklist (docs/RELEASING.md or a `just release-check \u003cversion\u003e` recipe) that runs 1–3 plus the existing version-consistency check (Cargo.toml / Chart.yaml version / appVersion) and the libs/clone.yaml pin, before the owner tags.\n\nAcceptance: CHANGELOG.md exists with Unreleased + backfilled tags; a tag's release body comes from it; `just screenshots` regenerates every committed screenshot from the mock UI; `just release-check` fails on stale screenshots, an Unreleased \"New\" entry without a docs link, or version mismatches. Prose follows docs/WRITING.md; claims follow docs/positioning.md.","files":null}]}